            10,
            10,
            10,
            10,
            10,
            10,
            10,
            10,
            10,
            10,
            10,
            10,
            10
          ],
          "ending": "Her friends teased her in March. By June nobody in the chat talked about XYZ any more. Her ₩10M is still there."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "quiz",
      "id": "q1",
      "concepts": [
        "leverage"
      ],
      "prompt": "Ji-woo invests ₩10M of her own and ₩10M borrowed. The price falls 30%. What happens to her own money?",
      "options": [
        "It falls 30%",
        "It falls 60%",
        "It falls 15%"
      ],
      "correctIndex": 1,
      "explanation": "She holds ₩20M of shares. A 30% fall is ₩6M, and all of it comes out of her own ₩10M, because the loan still has to be repaid in full: −60%."
    },
    {
      "type": "quiz",
      "id": "q2",
      "concepts": [
        "risk-capacity"
      ],
      "prompt": "Which money can Ji-woo put into a risky bet without hurting her life?",
      "options": [
        "Money she could lose completely and still pay rent and bills",
        "Her rent for next month",
        "Money borrowed at a low rate"
      ],
      "correctIndex": 0,
      "explanation": "Your [[risk-capacity]] is what you could lose without it changing your daily life. Rent money and borrowed money are not part of it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "t2",
      "title": "The loan stays",
      "body": "Borrowed money makes every move twice as big. A 30% fall takes 60% of her own money. The loan stays the same size either way."
    }
